  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="HHEBA1CD44839C108D1DAFD6DE3427BE45" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="HH22FBAEA0509E80B804A4341B1670898A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 0.9rem;"&gt;On July 18, 2018, in Docket No. PL17-1-001, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission dismissed the requests for rehearing and clarification of its revised policy statement on treatment of income taxes and provided guidance regarding the treatment of accumulated deferred income taxes in light of its revised policy. Inquiry Regarding the Commission's Policy for Recovery of Income Tax Costs, Order on Rehearing of Revised Policy Statement, 164 FERC 61,030 (Jul. 18, 2018). Pursuant to the guidance provided by the Commission in its July 18 Order, Algonquin Gas Transmission, LLC, a tax pass-through entity owned in part at that time by Spectra Energy Partners, LP, a master limited partnership, intends to remove any balances recorded in Accounts 190, 281, 282, and 283 of the Commission's Uniform System of Accounts, as well as excess ADIT that has been transferred to Account 254 and deficient ADIT that has been transferred to Account 182.3. Algonquin Gas Transmission, LLC has requested approval from the Chief Accountant of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission to implement the accounting entries necessary for removing these balances. Upon receipt of the Chief Accountant's approval, Algonquin Gas Transmission, LLC will reflect the removal of these balances in the annual and quarterly financing reporting required by Part 260 of the Commission's regulations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="HH582A4E700260C05D782FA2D6F218758A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="HHE60759687E403C6B3DE58B8464A791E0" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;Algonquin Gas Transmission, LLC continues to operate under its settlement rates under Docket No. RP24-781 that went into effect June 1, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
